WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.802
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Miley Cyrus.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.970
And we mentioned your family.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.271
You have a very loving,
supportive family.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.274
You also might have the world's
best godmother.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.275
-Yeah.
-Dolly Parton.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.343
-I'm pretty lucky.
-Yeah.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.345
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.681
-Yeah.
-You guys did a Super Bowl

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.015
commercial together.
-Yes.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.950
-You've done album work
together.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.686
-Which, it was amazing because,
you know, she was doing

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.555
it for the phones, yet every
time I coordinate and kind of

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.824
communicate with Dolly,
it's still through fax.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.824
-You have to --
-So I don't know

00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:27.493
what she's talking about.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.095
She's rarely on the phone.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.863
Next time we have to do it for
the fax machine.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.364
-So if you see her in a
commercial talking about

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:34.100
how great phones are, just know
that's some false advertising?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.203
-We do use the phone, but she
does a fax, and then someone

00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:41.340
scans the fax, and then they put
it into a text message,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.675
and then that gets sent to me.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.277
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.078
And it's always signed.

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:48.214
So now I've kind of started
my own version where I go

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:52.284
into the notes, and I've started
to try to make my own letters,

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:55.921
because there's something so
amazing just about a connection.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:58.290
It's just not casual, you know?

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.193
You know that she took the time.
-Yes.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.661
-To get out, I guess
her typewriter?

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:07.833
She also made me a demo one time
where she talks about being

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:11.171
super high-tech, but it was all
through a cassette,

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.073
which then she voice memoed onto
a flip phone,

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.142
which someone then put on to
the iPhone,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.476
which then got sent to me.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.080
-I like that she recorded it
on a flip phone,

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.780
then she Fedexed you
the flip phone?

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.949
-Yes. She has a phone.

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:25.617
She just doesn't use it,
I don't think.

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:28.821
I think someone uses it for her
and does the fax machine

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.823
through the phone.
-I mean, I should make it

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.526
very clear that while
we're joking about this,

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.194
nothing would make me happier
than if somebody

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.263
knocked on my door and said,
"Fax from Dolly Parton."

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.364
-Yeah.
-I'd be like --

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.667
-From like, a pink pigeon or
something.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.869
A flamingo probably delivers it.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.504
-It's just, like, a pigeon
knocking on the glass

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.772
outside the window.
-Yes.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.274
With long acrylic nails,
big boobs, and a blonde wig.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.275
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.409
The Dolly Pigeon.
-"I think that's

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:52.811
Dolly's pigeon." Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:55.415
-You did a cover of one of her
songs last time

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.783
you were on "SNL."

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.751
Did you tell her beforehand you
were going to do that,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.286
or did she find out?
-Well, that's another

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.621
Lorne thing. I didn't know
beforehand I was gonna do that.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.624
-Okay, so what day
does he let you know?

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.725
-That was on Saturday afternoon.
-No!

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:08.761
-Saturday, he gave you
a new song?

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:13.032
-Elon had a very long monologue,
and then they needed

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.401
to fill however long of time
that song is.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.669
-Oh, gotcha.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.938
-And didn't have the sketch in
between there and,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.673
"Miley, you're doing it."
-Wow.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:25.345
-So I kind of do -- I don't --
I guess my brand is kind of not

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.579
listening to anyone, but I
listen to Lorne Michaels.

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:29.515
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-That's a good guy to listen to.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:30.984
-Okay, gotcha, and then what did
Dolly think?

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.485
Did you get good feedback
via fax?

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.587
-Yes, I got a fax.
-Oh, good.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:38.991
-And she loved it, and she loves
when I introduce my fans

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:42.962
to music in a way that's
still me rather than --

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.064
Dolly doesn't
want anyone to copy/paste.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:48.867
She doesn't want anyone to just
sing her songs.

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:52.204
She wants them to infuse
themselves into her music,

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:55.241
because that's what I think has
made Dolly so loved is, again,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.342
the authenticity.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.810
I've taken a poll.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.880
I think Dolly is the most loved
person on the planet, right?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.715
-I think that that's probably
a safe bet.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:03.716
-Yeah.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.184
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:09.288
And again, it's just, she's been
so consistently caring and kind

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.756
and herself.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:14.227
And again, she didn't look like
the standard female

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:17.263
country music artist that was
polite and wearing long dresses.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.332
She had big hair and big boobs
and she's left this big mark

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:24.203
on the entire world that all of
us are just trying to fill her

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.605
crystalized shoes, which is
never going to happen.

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:30.176
-She was here once, and I went
backstage and I told her

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.478
my son's favorite song is
"Jolene."

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.080
And she was like, "Well, let's
Facetime him right now."

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.348
-How cool is that?

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:38.484
-So I Facetimed and she sang
"Jolene" to them.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.452
-No way.
-And now the bummer

00:03:40.452 --> 00:03:42.221
is they think that I can just
do that.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.056
-And that you can just call
Dolly whenever.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.791
-Because they have a lot of
thoughts, they're like,

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.094
"Can we just -- we'd love to
talk to Dolly about this."

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.530
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.632
-That's awesome.
-I know we were talking about

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:55.234
being back on the road,
touring again.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.503
I have to ask about this --
you were in an airplane

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.738
that was struck by lightning.
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.473
-What was that like?

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:03.109
-It was really scary.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:07.413
I was in my mom's lap, 'cause I
was pretty sure it didn't matter

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.714
about the seatbelts,
at this point.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:11.017
-Okay, gotcha. So when you were
in your mom's lap

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.519
because you were already afraid.
-I was crying and I was scared.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.322
And it was really very strange,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.591
because it
was unexpected weather,

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.260
and a few things that day --
when I woke up that morning,

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:24.130
I said, something just kind of
felt off and not quite right.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.300
And when we were on the plane,
it was completely unexpected.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.236
And yeah, we got struck by
lightning, which then, we had to

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.572
do this emergency landing
and we were in the middle

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.274
of South America, and I was
actually on my way to a show,

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:38.911
which by that point,
had been flooded and canceled.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:42.348
So there was just a lot going on
and everyone's like --

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:45.718
my guys in my band who are just
rock'n'rollers are, like,

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.754
"We got to get to the fans!
We got to still play the gig!"

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:52.491
I'm like, "Okay, no, we're in
the middle of, like, the forest

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.160
in a broken-down airplane.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.828
There's floods where we're
supposed to be going,

00:04:56.828 --> 00:04:58.264
the stage is sinking."

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:01.167
And so Brazil, where I was
playing a couple of days later,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.535
they were awesome.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:05.738
They let us in a couple of days
early and we were able

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.442
to kind of take a few days to
recuperate, just because all of

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.010
us were a little traumatized.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.978
Yeah, that makes sense.
That's very fair.

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.380
Well, we're glad you're safe.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.015
We've been very happy to have
you here.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.149
Thanks for everything.
-Thanks for having me.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:19.118
-And I can't wait --
-Club Fred!

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.786
Hey!

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.221
Miley Cyrus, everybody!

